<ResourceArticle page={resources.calcbar}>
  <p>Aubree Kendall’s original CalcBar 1.6 put a spreadsheet-style calculator in the Mac menu bar. Eva|Bar, previously called CalcBar2, is an independently maintained open-source calculator. Both apps let you open the bar with a shortcut, type a full expression, and lock the panel above other windows.</p>

  <h2>Rosetta and macOS 28 compatibility</h2>
  <p>We inspected CalcBar 1.6 (build 2.6) and confirmed its executable is Intel-only (<code>x86_64</code>). On Apple silicon, it needs Rosetta 2 to run through macOS 27. Starting with macOS 28, Apple says Rosetta will be limited to certain older games. Under that policy, this CalcBar build will no longer run on Apple silicon. Eva|Bar has a native Apple silicon download that runs without Rosetta.</p>
  <p class="resource-source">See <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/102527">Apple’s guidance on Rosetta and Intel-based apps</a>.</p>

  <h2>CalcBar 1.6 and Eva|Bar compared</h2>
  <table class="resource-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Feature</th><th scope="col">CalcBar 1.6</th><th scope="col">Eva|Bar</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Minimum macOS version</th><td>macOS 11.1</td><td>macOS 13</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Intel Macs</th><td>Native Intel build</td><td>Native Intel download</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Apple silicon</th><td>Requires Rosetta 2 through macOS 27. The Intel build will stop working on macOS 28.</td><td>Native Apple silicon download (<code>arm64</code>)</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Open from another app</th><td>Menu bar icon or customizable hotkey</td><td>Menu bar icon or customizable hotkey. The default is <kbd>Control–Shift–Space</kbd>.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Floating panel</th><td>Lock the panel to keep it visible</td><td>Lock the panel to keep it above your workspace</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Expression functions</th><td>Arithmetic, powers, averages, logarithms, and trigonometry</td><td>Arithmetic, powers, averages, logarithms, and trigonometry. Supports both <code>asin()</code> and <code>arcsin()</code>.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Distribution</th><td>Originally distributed through the Mac App Store</td><td>Free downloads through GitHub Releases, with source under the MIT license</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="resource-source">The original features are documented in the <a href="https://www.macupdater.org/app_updates/appinfo/com.AubreeCloud.CalcBar/index.html">archived app description</a>. The architecture and minimum macOS version come from the inspected app bundle.</p>

  <h2>Try your familiar CalcBar expressions</h2>
  <p>Open Eva|Bar and enter <code>avg(12,18,24)</code> for <strong>18</strong>, <code>log(81,3)</code> for <strong>4</strong>, or <code>sin(pi/2)</code> for <strong>1</strong>. <kbd>Return</kbd> copies the result to the clipboard. The <strong>f</strong> button opens the function reference.</p>

  <h2>Set up Eva|Bar on your Mac</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Check your macOS version and processor in <strong>Apple menu → About This Mac</strong>. Eva|Bar requires macOS 13 or later.</li>
    <li><a href="/#download">Download Eva|Bar</a> for your processor, unzip it, and move the app to Applications.</li>
    <li>Open <strong>… → Preferences</strong> to set your shortcut, decimal precision, and separators for displayed and copied results.</li>
  </ol>
</ResourceArticle>
